From aaa0150789f246ce8371b77ef7194a8349f31b76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:05:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): spend_promote operator action for a spend
 stop's named decision card [daveey]

A card stopped by the cumulative spend budget waits in triage for a recorded decision. When
no chat owns it, the stop names one supervisor decision card, whose worker cannot use the
board CLI; the operator courier offered only comment/move/unblock/label_publish, and an
unblock is not a decision. New operator action spend_promote {task_id, runs 1-20, episode,
decision_comment_id, reason}: only the card the stop's spend_budget_decision_ready producer
names, with its own operator decision comment made after the current stop, may release the
card. The home rechecks scope (current episode, producer, comment, human hold, parents)
inside one write transaction that moves triage->ready and records spend_budget_set (exactly
runs, existing cache-read override kept) plus promoted_manual carrying spend_budget. That
promoted_manual opens the new spend window, so the card gets exactly runs more runs.
Finite only (0/exempt refused); replay is already_applied via the operator_request_uid marker.

Proof: 21 new tests (legit target with exact 4-run window and re-stop on the 4th run,
unauthorized caller, home recheck of a superseded episode, stale caller run, foreign-home
routing, duplicate request, human hold at request and home, unblock refused and no
promoted_manual, decision-comment provenance, invalid ops, tool schema); 205 adjacent tests
pass. Window-rule replay over every hub kanban DB + sync-shadow: 39 real promoted_manual
rows, 0 carry spend_budget, so no existing window changes.
